---
/**
 * The per-row Save / Cancel cell that `initRowEdit()` drives.
 *
 * Extracted because it appeared **19 times across 3 pages** — and the copies had
 * drifted on the thing that matters most (Standardize sweep, 2026-08-18):
 *
 *   editable-grid    6 labelled, 4 unlabelled, 5 with a remove button
 *   field-editor     6 unlabelled
 *   inline-editing   3 unlabelled
 *
 * So 13 of 19 rows shipped a Save button whose accessible name was just
 * "Save" — and a table of them gives a screen-reader user six identical
 * buttons with nothing to tell them apart. axe cannot catch it, because the
 * buttons ARE named; they are just ambiguous, the same shape as the
 * placeholder-only-name finding in 27.5.
 *
 * `row` is therefore REQUIRED, not optional. The point of this component is
 * that the next page cannot forget the label, which is exactly what three
 * pages did when the markup was copy-pasted.
 *
 * The slot takes any extra row action (the editable grid's "Remove line"),
 * so the variants collapse into one definition without losing either.
 *
 * ── No `Unsaved` badge, and the state moved (roadmap 157.1, owner call) ──
 *
 * A dirty row said it three times: an amber tint, a 3px inset left edge, a
 * badge reading "Unsaved" — and then Save/Cancel appearing at all said it a
 * fourth. The row's own two visual channels are enough, and they already
 * survive forced-colors (the tint drops, the inset edge becomes a real
 * border).
 *
 * What the badge WAS carrying, and where it went: `data-row-state` is a data
 * attribute, invisible to assistive tech, so the badge was the only thing
 * announcing the state. `data-table.css` says this outright — a tone is "not
 * a substitute for a programmatic channel". So the meaning now rides the Save
 * button's accessible name, which exists only while the row is dirty. One
 * element instead of two, and the state travels on the control you act on.
 *
 * Icon-only, per the same owner call. The glyph is `--save` (a disk), NOT
 * `check-circle`: a tick on an ERP line reads as *approve*, a separate and
 * consequential action here.
 */
interface Props {
  /** The row's human name — "Bearing kit", "Credit limit". Used for the
      per-row accessible names, never displayed. */
  row: string;
}
const { row } = Astro.props;
---
<td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
  <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--icon bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-save
          aria-label={`Save ${row} — unsaved changes`} hidden>
    <span class="bo-icon bo-icon--save" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </button>
  <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--icon bo-btn--ghost" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel
          aria-label={`Discard changes to ${row}`} hidden>
    <span class="bo-icon bo-icon--close" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </button>
  <slot />
</td>
